{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_slice_1", "label": "Slice 1 \u2014 Local Ingest to a Visible Grid", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Phase 1's five subsystems are sequenced as a vertical slice rather than in dependency order, because dependency order leaves nothing visible until the third slice. The cost is that ingest is written synchronously here and moved behind the queue in slice 2 \u2014 a trigger change, not a rewrite."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_hash_first_short_circuit", "label": "Hash-First Short-Circuit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "BLAKE3 before anything else; a known hash skips parse, raster and write entirely. Scoped on library + part name + hash, not the hash alone: keying it on content alone let a content address decide a per-library write, and scanning six real STLs into an empty library reported six skips with the library still empty."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_cas", "label": "Blob CAS (BLAKE3, two-level hex sharding, ref_count)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_cpu_rasterized_thumbnail", "label": "CPU-Rasterized 512px WebP Thumbnail", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A GPU renderer makes output driver- and version-dependent, so byte-identical regeneration stops holding and golden-image tests become perceptual-diff tests with a tolerance. A Vulkan stack is also a large dependency and a driver-bug class that is miserable in air-gapped installs. Accepted cost: flat/matcap shading, adequate for triage."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_readonly_ingest_mount", "label": "Read-Only /ingest Mount", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The scan route takes no path argument, so no caller-supplied path ever reaches the filesystem and traversal is structurally impossible rather than defended against. Read-only means an ingest bug cannot damage the user's library."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_measurement_provenance", "label": "Per-Measurement Provenance Columns", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "volume_source and bbox_source sit beside the values they describe, because in Phase 2 a STEP revision has an analytic volume and a tessellated triangle count on the same row, and any single row-level flag must lie about one of them. triangle_count deliberately has no _source column: it cannot be analytic."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_role_split", "label": "LAPIDARY_ROLE Route Split", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Forced, not chosen: ingest must not run in the api process, whose image deliberately does not link lapidary-cad. Both containers run one binary with one router, so a role is the smallest thing that keeps the ingest path out of the open-path binary."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_source_store", "label": "SourceStore", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Obtainable only in the worker role. A dependency-graph rule cannot express the distinction, because depending on lapidary-storage is legitimate for derivatives; the distinction is which bytes, so it must be an API-level boundary."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_derivative_store", "label": "DerivativeStore", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Held by both roles: the api legitimately reads derivatives."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_lapidary_ingest", "label": "lapidary-ingest (L3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The scan route does not live in lapidary-api: a handler there needing MeshKernel would force lapidary-api -> lapidary-cad and put the CAD kernel back in the api image. A separate L3 crate makes the boundary a dependency edge rather than a runtime if."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_mesh_kernel", "label": "MeshKernel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "STL parsing and rasterization are geometry, so they sit behind the kernel boundary \u2014 ingest invokes the kernel, opening a part never does."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_library_table", "label": "library table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_part_table", "label": "part table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_revision_table", "label": "revision table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_file_table", "label": "file table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_table", "label": "blob table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_derivative_table", "label": "derivative table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_search_tsvector_stored", "label": "STORED tsvector Search Column", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Uses the simple configuration, not english or turkish: Phase 2 owns the real search design and part numbers must not be stemmed, so simple is the choice that does not pretend to have decided. The column exists now only because adding a generated column later is a table rewrite, and because PG 18's virtual default is easy to forget."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_default_library_seed", "label": "Migration-Seeded Default Library", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The scan route needs an id and nothing in the slice creates a library. A fixed uuid in a migration is the seam to watch: whichever slice adds a second library must replace the seed, not build beside it."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_orphan_blob_reap", "label": "Orphan Blob Reap Ordering", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The blob is written before the transaction and a failed transaction reaps it \u2014 the prototype leaked an orphan on exactly this path. The reap runs only on the branch that wrote bytes; reaping a blob another library's part references would be silent data loss, so the two branches are separate calls rather than one call with a flag."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_library_holds", "label": "PgBlobs::library_holds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Deliberately does not filter deleted_at, so a re-scan reports a soft-deleted part as skipped rather than resurrecting it."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_scan_not_transactional", "label": "A Scan Is Not Transactional Across Files", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "One malformed STL must not abort the walk. Failures are collected as {file, reason} and returned with a 200 summary, because a partial success is the accurate description. The prototype counted skips with no reasons at all, which is why a failed import there was undiagnosable."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_watertight_or_null_volume", "label": "Volume Is NULL When the Mesh Is Not Watertight", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Signed-volume integration over an open mesh returns a number that means nothing. 'Measurement must not lie' applied to the case where the honest answer is no answer."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_slice_1", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_hash_first_short_circuit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_hash_first_short_circuit", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_library_holds", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_library_holds", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_part_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_cas", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_table", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_source_store", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_cas", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_derivative_store", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_cas", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-phase-1-slice-1-ingest-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_mesh_kernel", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_cpu_rasterized_thumbnail", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpower